+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
+/*
+ * E-0007 experiment only. With none of the parameters given the module does
+ * what the driver does; what it records costs nothing until diag_on is set.
+ *
+ * Three things are in here.
+ *
+ * What can be switched to something else than the driver does, by
+ * parameters given when the module is loaded:
+ * exp_no_fc: 1 turns flow control off for the eight buffer manager ports on
+ * the CPU side.
+ * exp_tx_thread: 1 polls the TX completion rings in threads.
+ * exp_rx_softirq: 1 polls the RX rings in softirq context, not in threads.
+ * exp_combined: one poll for RX ring n and TX completion ring n, both of
+ * whose interrupts ask for it; 1 does the completions first, 2 the RX ring
+ * first. It runs where the RX polls run.
+ * exp_rx_weight, exp_tx_weight: how much one poll may do; 0 leaves 64.
+ * exp_cmpl_shift: TX queue q reports to completion ring q + this.
+ * exp_rx_mod, exp_tx_mod: the moderation timers.
+ * exp_rx_ring, exp_tx_ring, exp_txcmpl_ring: the ring sizes, powers of two.
+ * exp_bm_react, exp_bm_ceiling, exp_bm_weight, exp_bm_resume: the thresholds
+ * of the buffer manager's physical ports; exp_bm_group: the shared buffers.
+ * exp_raw_io: 1 reads and writes the registers of the rings without the
+ * register map and so without its lock.
+ * exp_page_idx: 1 notes a page's store index at the start of the page, where
+ * the hardware does not write, not in the pre-header.
+ * exp_sync_len: how much of a page is synced for the device when it goes
+ * back to the pool; 0 leaves the whole buffer.
+ * exp_rx_hardirq: 1 takes the frames out of an RX ring and puts the new
+ * buffers in from the interrupt handler itself; the frames wait in a queue of
+ * the driver's for the RX poll, which only hands them to the stack. When
+ * exp_rx_swq frames wait there the handler takes no more out of the ring and
+ * masks the interrupt until the poll has brought the queue down to half.
+ * exp_defer_irqs, exp_gro_flush_us: a poll that finds nothing left does not
+ * unmask its interrupt at once; the kernel calls it again after
+ * exp_gro_flush_us microseconds, and only after exp_defer_irqs such polls in a
+ * row that found nothing is the interrupt unmasked (the kernel's
+ * napi_defer_hard_irqs and gro_flush_timeout).
+ * exp_cpu_q_ceiling: the most buffers each of the host's four PPE queues may
+ * hold; 0 leaves what the driver writes. Below the threshold at which a port
+ * is told to pause, a queue whose RX ring is full drops its own frames and
+ * the port is not paused.
+ * exp_tx_hardirq: 1 deals with the completions from the interrupt handler
+ * itself. Both do at most exp_hardirq_budget slots for one interrupt.
+ *
+ * And by parameters that can be written while the driver runs:
+ * exp_tx_budget: how many completions one poll deals with at most; 0 leaves
+ * it to the budget.
+ * exp_rx_drop_port: UDP frames to this port or one of the 99 after it are
+ * dropped in the RX poll once their buffer has been replaced.
+ * exp_rx_delay_us: every RX poll first waits this long.
+ * exp_fill_lag: the hardware is told about this many fewer new buffers than
+ * the poll has put into the fill ring.
+ * exp_cons_lag: the hardware is told that this many fewer slots of the RX
+ * ring have been taken over than the poll has.
+ * exp_fill_every: n > 1 puts new buffers into the fill ring only in every
+ * n-th poll, for all the polls since, so that how many buffers a poll puts
+ * back is not how many slots it looks at.
+ * exp_tx_scan_extra: the completion poll walks the ports this many more
+ * times without doing anything.
+ *
+ * What the driver records about itself while diag_on is set: every poll
+ * (struct diag_poll), every packet sent by where it was sent from, and, with
+ * probes on the scheduler's and the interrupt tracepoints, where every CPU's
+ * time went and how long the NAPI threads waited for a CPU.
+ *
+ * A sampler that reads a list of registers at a fixed period from a timer
+ * interrupt, and a watcher that reads up to eight registers as fast as it
+ * can for a while and notes every change. Both read without the register map.
+ *
+ * All of it is read and steered through debugfs, directory ipq807x_diag.
+ */
